 ;; ── the measurement ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 :measurement
 {:probe "GET atproto.kotobase.net/xrpc/com.atproto.repo.describeRepo?repo=x"
  :why-this-probe
  "atproto is in `core/public-read-surfaces`, so a full shared-graph hydrate
   needs no credential. This is what made the measurement possible at all:
   sparql and cypher return 401 to a self-issued CACAO — they want an OPERATOR
   CACAO, and `KOTOBASE_MAINTENANCE_OPERATOR_DIDS` is owner-blocked. Measuring
   through them would have meant granting myself operator access to production,
   which is not a measurement decision."
  :returns-501 "The probe returns HTTP 501 MethodNotImplemented (`unsupported nsid: com.atproto.repo.describeRepo`) and that is EXPECTED: the shared-graph hydrate runs in the router BEFORE nsid dispatch, so the request performs the full hydrate and then declines the method. That is exactly why it works as a credential-free hydrate probe. Verified 2026-08-18 on ONE connection (curl --next, so the diagnostic lands on the same isolate): probe 501 in 3.9 s, then GET /_diag/hydrate reporting sampled true, block_gets 84, bytes 11462579, unfolded_txs 63. Separate connections land on different isolates and report sampled false, which is not evidence of anything."
  :method "wrangler tail --format json, each request carrying a ?probe=<uuid>
           marker so events match requests rather than being assumed to."
  :against "the deployed worker, which now carries the read-path hoist and the
            fetch coalescing landed 2026-08-17"
  :cpu-ms [2411 2539 2133 2410 2491 2178 2384 2114 2267 3689]
  :n 10 :median 2397 :mean 2462 :min 2114 :max 3689 :outcomes "10/10 ok"
  :cpu-over-wall "60-83% — this path is CPU-bound, not I/O-bound"
  :prior "2026-08-17, pre-fix, n=14: 2329-4416"}

 :correction-applied
 {:from 1976 :to 2397 :scale 1.2131
  :rule "The harness measures the DECOMPOSITION reliably; its absolute level is
         a Node proxy. Anchor the total to the measurement, preserve the
         measured proportions."
  :status "Every `:after` is now a MODELLED PROJECTION, not a measurement. Each
           hypothesis keeps `:after-harness` so the correction is auditable."
  :surprise "The proxy understated by 21%, not the several-fold iteration-01
             feared from its single pairing. n=1 was pessimistic, not optimistic."}

