 :what-changed
 {:order :unchanged
  :level "+12.0% — every price rises, because the thing being billed was
          under-counted, not because anything got worse"
  :crossover "0.93M -> 0.83M queries/month against one Neo4j Aura instance
              ($65/mo flat). kotobase's advantage window SHRANK."
  :the-real-move
  "h2 and h6 collapsed from a 4.12 gap to 0.18 — a near-tie. Under the proxy
   they were 4th and 5th with clear daylight; measured, choosing between them
   is no longer a cost question. h2 is deployed, reversible and one write from
   firing; h6 is owner-blocked and irreversible. The judge now says: take h2,
   and stop treating h6 as a cost decision at all."
  :honest-note
  "Closing the loop's own dominant uncertainty did NOT reorder the roadmap.
   That is worth recording — the measurement was still correct to take, but a
   loop that reports every measurement as decisive is flattering itself."}

 ;; ── the finding that outranks the ranking ───────────────────────────────────
 :zero-traffic
 {:observation "Twelve consecutive GET /_diag/hydrate returned `sampled: false`
                — twelve isolates, none of which had ever hydrated."
  :meaning "There are no organic served reads on this graph. This loop prices a
            served read on a graph that currently serves none."
  :why-it-is-not-a-defect-of-the-loop
  "iteration-01 already said it: 'Today's value is the unit-economics crossover,
   not saved CPU on traffic that is not there.' The measurement confirms it
   rather than discovering it. What is new is that it is now countable: 12/12,
   not an impression from a five-minute tail."
  :consequence
  "The ranking is FOR the crossover argument — at what volume kotobase beats a
   flat-rate graph database — not for a latency or bill that anyone is paying
   today. Any roadmap item justified by 'it saves CPU in production' is
   currently justified by nothing."}

 :also-fixed
 {:what "The engine could not be loaded from where it lived."
  :detail "ns `kotobase-performance.cost-coscientist` resolves to the directory
           `kotobase_performance`, but the file sat in `kotobase-performance/`
           beside the .edn receipts. `(require ...)` failed. iteration-01 was
           produced from some other layout, so the landed engine had never been
           run in place."
  :fix "Moved to `src/kotobase_performance/` with a `run.cljs` beside the
        receipts. Verified: the engine reproduces iteration-01's numbers exactly
        (70.06 / h1 29.26 / h7 40.92 / h2 42.62 / h6 46.74) before the
        correction was applied, which is what makes the diff above attributable
        to the measurement rather than to the move."}

 :seed-for-next
 "Two candidates, and they are not the same kind of question.

  (a) h7, the top UNBLOCKED build item: `decode2` is
      `(edn/read-string (edn/read-string v_edn))` on every value of every doc on
      every request, and the hydrate decodes the whole LocalStore map when a
      point read addresses one key. The B half is 1,735 of 2,397 measured ms.
      Risk is that the LocalStore contract is synchronous and plain — deferring
      values changes a shape other code reads.

  (b) Whether to keep pricing this at all. The crossover is the only live
      argument, and it rests on Aura's $65/mo, which is second-hand because the
      vendor page returned 403. A judge whose comparator is unverified is one
      403 away from being decorative."}
